VERDICT: REJECTED

The project builds successfully, but the claimed end-to-end seven-role workflow is not functionally correct at deployment. Regional directors collect and validate per-tax-center allocations, yet `finalizePlan` discards those allocations and calls `generateCases` with only the original regional distribution. Generated cases are instead round-robin assigned among tax centers, so approved regional allocation decisions are not honored. It also caps generation at eight cases per audit type per region, meaning a finalized plan with 1,400–1,550 planned cases yields at most 240 cases; the deployed workload therefore does not match the approved plan.

Additionally, the Tax Center dashboard's status tabs do not affect the displayed rows: `tab` is updated but never applied to `filtered`, so every tab shows the same filtered case set.

Security: none observed relevant to this task; this is clearly a browser-local demo and real authentication/backend persistence are separately proposed tasks.

Next actions:
1. Generate cases from each region's submitted `taxCenterAllocations` (with an explicit fallback only where appropriate), preserving every approved allocation by audit type and tax center.
2. Remove or make explicit any demo cap; deployment must reconcile generated cases to `plan.totalCases` and surface validation failures.
3. Apply the selected status tab as an additional case filter, or remove nonfunctional tabs.

VERDICT: REJECTED
